%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 75e7bea227aaf2b499307efe1ddc0480, type: 3}
  m_Name: AsterDialog
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::NPCDialog
  NPCName: Aster
  DialogLines:
  - text: "Chief\u2026 you came through the portal!"
    isQuestion: 0
    choices: []
  - text: Good. That means the portal is still holding together.
    isQuestion: 0
    choices: []
  - text: "This one here links the upper wards to the deep sector\u2026 and further
      still, if the chain is restored."
    isQuestion: 0
    choices: []
  - text: But the storm damaged more than its transport function.
    isQuestion: 0
    choices: []
  - text: The portal used to recognize those who passed through it.
    isQuestion: 0
    choices: []
  - text: "Not just where they came from\u2026 but who was returning."
    isQuestion: 0
    choices: []
  - text: "A traveler who stepped through once\u2026 would be known if they came
      again."
    isQuestion: 0
    choices: []
  - text: Now, every arrival feels the same to it.
    isQuestion: 0
    choices: []
  - text: "You could pass through a hundred times\u2026 and the system would greet
      you as a stranger each time."
    isQuestion: 0
    choices: []
  - text: "That makes it difficult to tell whether the same explorer is making progress\u2026
      or if new ones keep failing in the dark."
    isQuestion: 0
    choices: []
  - text: "If I restore the portal\u2019s memory, it will mark your passage\u2026
      and remember you when you return."
    isQuestion: 0
    choices: []
  - text: It will not change your journey. Only whether the system knows it is still
      you walking it.
    isQuestion: 0
    choices: []
  - text: "Tell me, Chief\u2026 shall I restore the portal\u2019s memory?"
    isQuestion: 1
    choices:
    - choiceText: "Restore the portal\u2019s memory."
      nextDialogIndex: 13
    - choiceText: Leave it as it is.
      nextDialogIndex: 14
  - text: Understood. The gate will remember you the next time you step through.
    isQuestion: 0
    choices: []
  - text: Very well. Then every return will be treated as a first arrival.
    isQuestion: 0
    choices: []
